You said:
is we want to do anything manullay on our own to scrap metrics from otel collector if yes please explain for very beginners

ChatGPT said:
Perfect question 👍 — and I like that you asked it from a beginner point of view.
Let’s slow this down and make it crystal clear, no assumptions.

🔑 The honest answer first
Yes, you must do ONE manual thing so Prometheus can scrape metrics from the OpenTelemetry Collector.

But don’t worry 😄 — it’s very small, very safe, and very standard.

You do NOT write scripts
You do NOT curl metrics in production
You do NOT touch Prometheus internals

You only tell Prometheus WHERE to scrape

🧠 Beginner mental model (remember this)
OTEL Collector → exposes metrics at /metrics
Prometheus     → needs to know that URL
Prometheus will NOT auto-guess OTEL.

✅ What exactly must be done manually?
There are 3 simple steps.

🪜 Step 1: Make sure OTEL exposes metrics (already done once)
Inside OTEL config:

exporters:
  prometheus:
    endpoint: "0.0.0.0:8889"
This creates:

http://otel-collector:8889/metrics
✔️ Nothing else here

🪜 Step 2: Expose OTEL metrics via Kubernetes Service
Prometheus scrapes Services, not pods.

Create this file:

📄 otel-metrics-service.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: otel-collector-metrics
  namespace: observability
  labels:
    app: otel-collector
spec:
  selector:
    app: otel-collector
  ports:
    - name: metrics
      port: 8889
      targetPort: 8889
Apply:

kubectl apply -f otel-metrics-service.yaml
👉 This step is MANDATORY and done once

🪜 Step 3: Tell Prometheus to scrape it (ServiceMonitor)
This is the ONLY place beginners get confused.

What is ServiceMonitor?
Think of it as:

“Hey Prometheus, please scrape THIS service”

📄 otel-servicemonitor.yaml
apiVersion: monitoring.coreos.com/v1
kind: ServiceMonitor
metadata:
  name: otel-collector
  namespace: observability
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: otel-collector
  namespaceSelector:
    matchNames:
      - observability
  endpoints:
    - port: metrics
      path: /metrics
      interval: 15s
Apply:

kubectl apply -f otel-servicemonitor.yaml
🎉 Done. No more manual work forever.

🔍 How do I know it’s working?
Check Prometheus UI
kubectl port-forward svc/prometheus-kube-prometheus-prometheus 9090 -n observability
Open:

http://localhost:9090
Go to:
👉 Status → Targets

You should see:

otel-collector-metrics   UP
🧪 Beginner-friendly verification commands
kubectl get svc -n observability
kubectl get servicemonitor -n observability
curl otel-collector.observability.svc.cluster.local:8889/metrics
If this works → Prometheus will scrape.

🚫 Things you DO NOT do (important)
❌ Do NOT edit Prometheus config manually
❌ Do NOT use NodePort
❌ Do NOT scrape Pod IPs
❌ Do NOT run cron jobs

🏭 Why this is production safe
Reason	Explanation
Declarative	YAML stored in Git
Auto-recovery	Pods change, Service stays
Scalable	Multiple OTEL replicas
Secure	Namespace-scoped
🧠 One-liner to remember
Prometheus scrapes Services.
ServiceMonitor tells it which ones.

That’s it.

