Use --debug flag to render out invalid YAML

ChatGPT said:
Very good 👍 this is a normal Helm chart validation error — nothing is broken.

The error says:

[ERROR] 'image.repository' must be set.
This means:

👉 The OpenTelemetry Helm chart requires you to explicitly define which container image to use.
Newer versions do not assume defaults.

🎯 Why This Happens
The opentelemetry-collector chart expects this in values:

image:
  repository: <required>
  tag: <optional>
If not provided → Helm stops rendering.

This is intentional (security + clarity).

✅ Solution 1 (Quick Fix for Practice in Minikube)
Run template with image override:

helm template otel open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector \
  --namespace observability \
  --set image.repository="otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib" \
  > otel.yaml
Now it should generate successfully.

✅ Solution 2 (Better Production Way — Using values file)
Step 1 — Create otel-values.yaml

image:
  repository: otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib
  tag: latest
  pullPolicy: IfNotPresent

mode: deployment

config:
  receivers:
    otlp:
      protocols:
        grpc:
        http:

  exporters:
    debug:

  service:
    pipelines:
      traces:
        receivers: [otlp]
        exporters: [debug]
Step 2 — Template using values file:

helm template otel open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector \
  --namespace observability \
  -f otel-values.yaml \
  > otel.yaml
This is the correct DevOps workflow.

🔎 Why Prometheus Chart Didn’t Give This Error?
Because:

kube-prometheus-stack
Has default image values.

But OpenTelemetry chart requires explicit image definition.

🧠 How To Discover Required Fields Before Error
You can inspect default values:

helm show values open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector
Look for:

image:
You’ll see repository is empty.

🧪 If Still Error, Use Debug Mode
helm template otel open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector \
  --namespace observability \
  --set image.repository="otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib" \
  --debug
This prints internal rendering steps.

🎯 Final Clean Command for Minikube Practice
Use this:

helm template otel open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector \
  --namespace observability \
  --set image.repository=otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib \
  --set mode=deployment \
  > otel.yaml
Now open:

less otel.yaml
You’ll see:

Deployment

Service

ConfigMap

RBAC

ServiceAccount

🚀 Important DevOps Lesson
When Helm gives error like:

must be set
Always:

1️⃣ Run helm show values
2️⃣ Create your own values.yaml
3️⃣ Pass with -f values.yaml

Never depend on defaults blindly.

