  --namespace observability \
  --set image.repository=otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib \
  --set mode=deployment \
  > otel.yaml
This should now work.

🧠 Why This Is Happening
Newer versions of the OTEL Helm chart removed defaults to prevent:

Accidental production misconfiguration

Running wrong mode unknowingly

Security issues

So now it forces you to explicitly define:

image.repository

mode

✅ Recommended Beginner Values File (Better Way)
Instead of long --set flags, create:

📄 otel-values.yaml
mode: deployment

image:
  repository: otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib
  tag: latest
  pullPolicy: IfNotPresent

config:
  receivers:
    otlp:
      protocols:
        grpc:
        http:

  exporters:
    debug:

  service:
    pipelines:
      traces:
        receivers: [otlp]
        exporters: [debug]
Then template:

helm template otel open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector \
  --namespace observability \
  -f otel-values.yaml \
  > otel.yaml
This is the proper DevOps way.

🔎 If You Want to See What Fields Are Required
Run:

helm show values open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector
Search for:

mode:
image:
You’ll notice they have no default values.

🎯 Which Mode Should You Use?
For Minikube practice:

mode: deployment
For production high-traffic cluster:

mode: daemonset
Why?

DaemonSet = one collector per node = better performance.

But for learning → deployment is simpler.

🚀 Final Working Command For You
Use this exactly:

