before deploying kube-prometheus-stack what important things we need to check please tell me if want to install kube-prometheus-stack

ChatGPT said:
Excellent question 👏 — this is exactly how a production DevOps engineer should think before installing kube-prometheus-stack.

This chart is very powerful and very heavy. If installed blindly, it can:

Consume high memory

Create cluster-wide RBAC

Install CRDs

Expose services publicly

Impact other teams

So here is a real production checklist before installing.

✅ 1️⃣ Check Cluster Capacity (Very Important)
kube-prometheus-stack installs:

Prometheus

Alertmanager

Grafana

node-exporter (DaemonSet)

kube-state-metrics

CRDs

Admission webhooks

It can consume:

2–4 GB RAM minimum

1–2 CPU cores

Check cluster resources:
kubectl top nodes
If you're on:

Minikube → give at least 6–8GB RAM

Small prod cluster → verify enough free memory

✅ 2️⃣ Review CRDs (Cluster-wide Impact)
This chart installs CRDs like:

Prometheus

ServiceMonitor

PodMonitor

Alertmanager

Check CRDs first:

helm template prometheus prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack \
  --namespace monitoring > kps.yaml

grep -i CustomResourceDefinition kps.yaml
CRDs affect entire cluster — not just namespace.

In production:

Install CRDs carefully

Usually done once

✅ 3️⃣ Review RBAC Permissions
Search for:

grep -i ClusterRole kps.yaml
grep -i cluster-admin kps.yaml
Check if it creates:

ClusterRole

ClusterRoleBinding

Make sure it's not over-permissive.

✅ 4️⃣ Disable What You Don’t Need
By default it installs everything.

In production, many companies disable:

grafana:
  enabled: false

alertmanager:
  enabled: false
If they already use external Grafana.

✅ 5️⃣ Check Service Type (Security Critical)
By default:

Grafana service might be:

type: ClusterIP
But sometimes people change to:

type: LoadBalancer
Before installing, confirm:

helm show values prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack | grep type:
Never expose Prometheus publicly without auth.

✅ 6️⃣ Set Resource Limits
By default Prometheus may not have strict limits.

In production, you MUST set:

prometheus:
  prometheusSpec:
    resources:
      requests:
        memory: 2Gi
        cpu: 500m
      limits:
        memory: 4Gi
        cpu: 1
Otherwise it may consume all node memory.

✅ 7️⃣ Storage Configuration (Very Important)
Prometheus stores metrics locally.

Check:

prometheus:
  prometheusSpec:
    storageSpec:
If not configured:

It may use emptyDir → data lost on restart.

In production:

storageSpec:
  volumeClaimTemplate:
    spec:
      storageClassName: standard
      accessModes: ["ReadWriteOnce"]
      resources:
        requests:
          storage: 50Gi
✅ 8️⃣ Retention Period
Default retention may be 15d.

Check:

prometheus:
  prometheusSpec:
    retention: 15d
Longer retention = more storage usage.

✅ 9️⃣ Namespace Isolation
Never install in default.

Create dedicated namespace:

kubectl create namespace monitoring
✅ 10️⃣ Version Pinning
Never install latest blindly.

Check available versions:

helm search repo kube-prometheus-stack --versions
Install specific version:

helm install prometheus prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack \
  --version 56.6.2 \
  -n monitoring
🏢 Real Production Workflow
Pull chart

Review values.yaml

Create custom values-prod.yaml

Limit resources

Configure storage

Review RBAC

Install via GitOps

Monitor memory usage

