You said:

Namespace

what is meaning of this
namespace: {{ template "kube-prometheus-stack.namespace" . }}

ChatGPT said:
Good 👍 this is a Helm templating syntax, not normal YAML.

You saw:

namespace: {{ template "kube-prometheus-stack.namespace" . }}
Let’s break it clearly.

🧠 This Is NOT Kubernetes YAML
This is Helm template code written in Go template language.

Helm processes this BEFORE creating final YAML.

After rendering, it becomes something like:

namespace: monitoring
🔎 Break It Down
1️⃣ {{ ... }}
This means:

"Helm, execute this template logic here"

2️⃣ template
template is a Helm function.

It calls a named template defined somewhere else (usually in _helpers.tpl).

3️⃣ "kube-prometheus-stack.namespace"
This is the name of a helper template.

It is usually defined inside:

templates/_helpers.tpl
Inside that file you’ll find something like:

{{- define "kube-prometheus-stack.namespace" -}}
{{ .Release.Namespace }}
{{- end }}
This means:

Return the namespace where Helm is installing the chart.

4️⃣ The dot .
. represents the current Helm context object.

It contains:

.Values

.Release

.Chart

.Capabilities

So here:

template "kube-prometheus-stack.namespace" .
Means:

Call that helper template and pass full context.

🎯 What It Finally Becomes
If you install like:

helm install prometheus . -n monitoring
Helm renders:

namespace: monitoring
🏗 Why Use Template Instead of Hardcoding?
Instead of writing:

namespace: monitoring
Helm makes it dynamic.

If you install in another namespace:

helm install prometheus . -n observability
It will automatically render:

namespace: observability
📌 Where To See This Definition?
Run:

grep -R "kube-prometheus-stack.namespace" .
You’ll see it's defined in _helpers.tpl.

🧠 Important Helm Concept
Helm charts use:

templates/ → real k8s manifests

_helpers.tpl → reusable logic blocks

The line you saw is calling a reusable helper function.

🚀 If You Want To See Rendered Version
Run:

helm template test . -n monitoring
You’ll see actual namespace value instead of template code.

🎯 Simple Mental Model
Think of it like:

Helm template code = Java method call
Rendered YAML = Method output

