You said:

Namespace: `observability`

but we deploy prometheuse on monitoring namsescpace now?

ChatGPT said:
Good catch 👌 — yes, earlier we deployed:

kube-prometheus-stack → monitoring namespace

OpenTelemetry Collector → observability namespace

That is completely fine ✅ and actually common in production.

Let me explain clearly how this works and what you must configure.

🧠 Is It OK To Use Different Namespaces?
Yes ✔

Namespaces are just logical isolation.

Pods in different namespaces can still communicate using:

<service-name>.<namespace>.svc.cluster.local
🎯 Current Setup
Component	Namespace
Prometheus	monitoring
OTEL Collector	observability
Now question becomes:

👉 How does Prometheus scrape metrics from OTEL in another namespace?

✅ Option 1 — Expose OTEL Metrics Endpoint Properly
OpenTelemetry Collector exposes metrics at:

:8888/metrics
So Prometheus must scrape:

otel-collector.observability.svc.cluster.local:8888
🎯 Production-Ready Way (Using ServiceMonitor)
Since kube-prometheus-stack installs Prometheus Operator,
you should create a ServiceMonitor in monitoring namespace.

Example:

apiVersion: monitoring.coreos.com/v1
kind: ServiceMonitor
metadata:
  name: otel-collector-monitor
  namespace: monitoring
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app.kubernetes.io/name: opentelemetry-collector
  namespaceSelector:
    matchNames:
      - observability
  endpoints:
    - port: metrics
      path: /metrics
      interval: 30s
Important part:

namespaceSelector:
  matchNames:
    - observability
This tells Prometheus:

👉 "Scrape service from another namespace"

🧠 But Wait — Does OTEL Service Expose Metrics Port?
Check OTEL service:

kubectl get svc -n observability
It must expose port 8888.

If not, modify your values-prod.yaml:

ports:
  metrics:
    enabled: true
    containerPort: 8888
    servicePort: 8888
Then upgrade:

helm upgrade otel . -n observability -f values-prod.yaml
🎯 How Traffic Flows
Prometheus (monitoring namespace)
↓
ServiceMonitor
↓
OTEL service in observability namespace
↓
Scrapes :8888/metrics

🚨 Important Production Rule
Prometheus by default only watches its own namespace.

So in kube-prometheus-stack values you must ensure:

prometheus:
  prometheusSpec:
    serviceMonitorSelectorNilUsesHelmValues: false
Otherwise it may ignore external ServiceMonitors.

🔥 Alternative (Simpler For Practice)
If you're just learning:

You can deploy both in same namespace:

monitoring
That removes cross-namespace complexity.

🏢 Real Production Architecture
Many companies use:

monitoring → Prometheus stack
observability → OTEL + Loki + Tempo
prod → applications
Cross-namespace monitoring is normal.

🎯 Final Answer
Yes, Prometheus in monitoring namespace
and OTEL in observability namespace
is perfectly fine.

You just need:

✔ OTEL service exposing 8888
✔ ServiceMonitor with namespaceSelector
✔ Prometheus configured to watch ServiceMonitors

