ChatGPT said:
Yes ✅ — you are thinking correctly.

Let’s clarify properly and precisely.

🎯 Is ServiceMonitor a Custom Object?
👉 Yes.

ServiceMonitor is a Custom Resource (CR).

It is NOT a default Kubernetes object like:

Pod

Service

Deployment

It exists because kube-prometheus-stack installs a CRD.

🧠 Who Creates This CRD?
When you install:

kube-prometheus-stack

It installs several CRDs, including:

ServiceMonitor

PodMonitor

Prometheus

Alertmanager

PrometheusRule

You can verify:

kubectl get crds | grep monitor
You will see something like:

servicemonitors.monitoring.coreos.com
podmonitors.monitoring.coreos.com
🎯 What Actually Happens Internally?
The chart installs:

Prometheus Operator

This operator:

Watches for ServiceMonitor objects

Watches for PodMonitor objects

Automatically updates Prometheus config

So when you create:

kind: ServiceMonitor
You are not configuring Prometheus manually.

You are telling:

👉 Prometheus Operator
👉 “Please configure Prometheus to scrape this service”

The operator updates Prometheus behind the scenes.

🧠 So Your Statement:
It only uses custom resources created by Prometheus stack right?

✔ YES.

Without installing kube-prometheus-stack (or Prometheus Operator), this will fail:

kind: ServiceMonitor
Because Kubernetes won't know what ServiceMonitor is.

🎯 How It Works End-to-End
1️⃣ kube-prometheus-stack installs CRDs
2️⃣ Prometheus Operator runs in cluster
3️⃣ You create ServiceMonitor
4️⃣ Operator detects it
5️⃣ Operator updates Prometheus config
6️⃣ Prometheus starts scraping

All automatic.

🔥 Important Production Note
If you delete kube-prometheus-stack:

❗ CRDs remain in cluster unless manually removed
❗ ServiceMonitors will still exist
❗ But no operator will process them

🧠 Quick Verification
Check CRDs:

kubectl get crd | grep monitoring.coreos.com
Check ServiceMonitor instances:

kubectl get servicemonitor -A
🎯 Final Clear Answer
✔ ServiceMonitor is a Custom Resource
✔ It is created via CRD installed by kube-prometheus-stack
✔ It only works because Prometheus Operator watches it
✔ Without the operator, it does nothing

