You said:
please show difference between 
Difference between ServiceMonitor vs PodMonitor

ChatGPT said:
Excellent question 👏 — this is a very important concept when using kube-prometheus-stack.

Both ServiceMonitor and PodMonitor are Custom Resources installed by:

kube-prometheus-stack

Managed by Prometheus Operator

But they are used in different scenarios.

🎯 High-Level Difference
Feature	ServiceMonitor	PodMonitor
Scrapes	Kubernetes Service	Directly scrapes Pods
Uses	Service selector	Pod label selector
Most common	✅ Yes	Less common
Works with	Stable service endpoints	Dynamic pods
🧠 1️⃣ ServiceMonitor (Most Used)
What It Does
Prometheus scrapes metrics via:

Service → Endpoints → Pods
So flow is:

Prometheus
→ ServiceMonitor
→ Service
→ Pods

Example Use Case
You have:

kind: Service
metadata:
  name: my-app
Your app exposes metrics at:

:8080/metrics
Then you create:

apiVersion: monitoring.coreos.com/v1
kind: ServiceMonitor
metadata:
  name: my-app-monitor
  namespace: monitoring
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: my-app
  namespaceSelector:
    matchNames:
      - production
  endpoints:
    - port: http
      path: /metrics
      interval: 30s
This tells Prometheus:

👉 “Find service with label app=my-app
👉 Scrape its endpoints”

When To Use ServiceMonitor?
✅ When application exposes metrics through a Service
✅ When you want stable, load-balanced scraping
✅ Standard microservice setup

This is 90% of use cases.

🧠 2️⃣ PodMonitor
What It Does
Prometheus scrapes directly:

Pod IP → Pod port
Flow:

Prometheus
→ PodMonitor
→ Pods

No service involved.

Example
apiVersion: monitoring.coreos.com/v1
kind: PodMonitor
metadata:
  name: my-app-pod-monitor
  namespace: monitoring
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: my-app
  namespaceSelector:
    matchNames:
      - production
  podMetricsEndpoints:
    - port: metrics
      path: /metrics
      interval: 30s
When To Use PodMonitor?
✅ When no Service exists
✅ For DaemonSets
✅ For node-level agents
✅ For sidecars
✅ When scraping internal-only pod ports

🎯 Real Example in Your Case
OpenTelemetry Collector:

If OTEL exposes a Service:

→ Use ServiceMonitor

If OTEL runs as DaemonSet without Service:

→ Use PodMonitor

🔥 Production Recommendation
Use ServiceMonitor whenever possible.

Why?

Stable DNS

Cleaner architecture

Service abstraction

Works better with scaling

PodMonitor is for advanced cases.

🎯 Internal Technical Difference
Feature	ServiceMonitor	PodMonitor
Uses	endpoints field	podMetricsEndpoints
Discovers via	Endpoints object	Direct Pod list
Load balancing	Through Service	No
Resilient to restart	Yes	Depends
🧠 Visual Comparison
ServiceMonitor
Prometheus
    ↓
Service
    ↓
Pods
PodMonitor
Prometheus
    ↓
Pods directly
🚀 What Big Companies Do?
Mostly:

✔ ServiceMonitor for apps
✔ PodMonitor for infra agents (node-exporter, etc.)

🎯 Final Summary
If You Have	Use
Service object	ServiceMonitor
Only Pods	PodMonitor
DaemonSet	PodMonitor
Normal Deployment	ServiceMonitor
You are now understanding Prometheus Operator architecture deeply 👏

