Error: INSTALLATION FAILED: execution error at (loki/templates/validate.yaml:31:4): You have more than zero replicas configured for both the single binary and simple scalable targets. If this was intentional change the deploymentMode to the transitional 'SingleBinary<->SimpleScalable' mode
avenues@AVN-ITG-0264:~/opt/git-hub-repos/kuberne

ChatGPT said:
Perfect 👍 this error is very common with newer versions of the
loki

Let’s understand it properly.

❌ Why This Error Happens
Error:

You have more than zero replicas configured for both the single binary and simple scalable targets.
In new Loki charts:

There are multiple deployment modes:

SingleBinary

SimpleScalable

Distributed

SingleBinary<->SimpleScalable (migration mode)

Even if you set:

deploymentMode: SingleBinary
The chart still has default replicas set for read, write, or backend (SimpleScalable mode).

So Helm sees:

singleBinary.replicas > 0 ✅

read/write/backend replicas > 0 ❌ (default values)

And it fails.

✅ Correct Production Values (Fixed Version)
You must explicitly disable SimpleScalable components.

Replace your values-prod.yaml with this corrected version:

deploymentMode: SingleBinary

loki:
  auth_enabled: false

  commonConfig:
    replication_factor: 1

  storage:
    type: filesystem

  schemaConfig:
    configs:
      - from: 2024-01-01
        store: boltdb-shipper
        object_store: filesystem
        schema: v13
        index:
          prefix: loki_index_
          period: 24h

  storage_config:
    boltdb_shipper:
      active_index_directory: /var/loki/index
      cache_location: /var/loki/cache
      shared_store: filesystem
    filesystem:
      directory: /var/loki/chunks

  limits_config:
    retention_period: 168h
    ingestion_rate_mb: 10
    ingestion_burst_size_mb: 20

# ✅ Enable only SingleBinary
singleBinary:
  replicas: 1
  persistence:
    enabled: true
    storageClass: standard   # change if needed
    accessModes:
      - ReadWriteOnce
    size: 20Gi

# ❌ Disable SimpleScalable components explicitly
read:
  replicas: 0

write:
  replicas: 0

backend:
  replicas: 0

resources:
  requests:
    cpu: 200m
    memory: 512Mi
  limits:
    cpu: 500m
    memory: 1Gi

service:
  type: ClusterIP
  port: 3100
🚀 Now Install Again
helm install loki . \
  -n observability \
  -f values-prod.yaml
