⚠ 90% of the time CrashLoopBackOff in OpenTelemetry Collector is caused by:

Invalid exporter configuration

Wrong endpoint

Invalid YAML structure

Unsupported exporter (like loki misconfigured)

Pipeline references exporter that does not exist

🔎 Based On Your Setup (Very Likely Issue)
You earlier configured:

exporters:
  loki:
    endpoint: http://loki.observability.svc.cluster.local:3100/loki/api/v1/push
⚠ Problem:

In newer collector versions (0.145.0), the Loki exporter is NOT enabled unless:

You use contrib image (you are ✔)

But the config must follow correct format

Correct Loki exporter format for 0.145.0:

exporters:
  loki:
    endpoint: http://loki.observability.svc.cluster.local:3100/loki/api/v1/push
    tls:
      insecure: true
If you forgot tls.insecure and Loki is HTTP → collector crashes.

🔥 Second Very Common Issue
If you defined exporter name like this:

exporters:
  otlp/tempo:
Then in pipeline you MUST use exact same name:

exporters: [otlp/tempo]
If mismatch → crash.

🔥 Third Common Issue
Metrics pipeline cannot have empty exporters.

If you wrote:

metrics:
  receivers: [otlp]
  processors: [memory_limiter, batch]
  exporters: []
Collector WILL crash.

Metrics pipeline must have at least one exporter.

For example:

exporters:
  prometheus:
    endpoint: "0.0.0.0:8889"
🎯 Most Likely Root Cause
From your pod info:

Args:
  --config=/conf/relay.yaml
Your config file name is relay.yaml.

If that file inside ConfigMap is invalid → collector exits immediately.

Check config:

kubectl get configmap -n observability otel-opentelemetry-collector -o yaml
