Perfect 👍 this log clearly shows the REAL issue now.

❌ Actual Error
listen tcp 10.244.120.75:8888: bind: address already in use
This means:

👉 Port 8888 is already being used
👉 OTEL is trying to bind to 8888 again
👉 So collector crashes

🎯 Why This Is Happening
Look at your logs carefully:

Serving metrics {"address": "10.244.120.75:8888"}
Serving metrics {"address": ":8888"}
Port 8888 is already used by:

👉 OpenTelemetry internal telemetry endpoint

By default,
OpenTelemetry Collector
uses 8888 for its own internal metrics.

Then you also exposed:

prometheus:
  endpoint: "0.0.0.0:8888"
So:

Internal telemetry → 8888

Prometheus exporter → 8888

🔥 Conflict → crash.

✅ Proper Fix (Very Important)
We must change Prometheus exporter port.

Use a DIFFERENT port like:

8889
✅ Correct Prometheus Exporter Config
Change this:

prometheus:
  endpoint: "0.0.0.0:8888"
To:

prometheus:
  endpoint: "0.0.0.0:8889"
✅ Also Update Helm Ports Section
In your values.yaml, make sure:

ports:
  metrics:
    enabled: true
    containerPort: 8889
    servicePort: 8889
    protocol: TCP
NOT 8888.

🚀 Why 8888 Is Special
8888 = OTEL internal telemetry
8889 = Prometheus exporter (recommended)

This is best practice.

🔁 Now Upgrade
helm upgrade otel . -n observability -f values-prod.yaml
