Your root cause is clearly this line:

error: listen tcp :8888: bind: address already in use
Port 8888 is already occupied, and your OpenTelemetry Collector is trying to bind to it again.

From your logs:

Serving metrics {"address": "10.244.120.75:8888"}
Serving metrics {"address": ":8888"}
That means two components are trying to use port 8888.

✅ Why This Happens
In OpenTelemetry Collector:

Port 8888 is typically used for:

Internal collector telemetry (service.telemetry.metrics)

OR Prometheus exporter

You currently have both trying to bind to :8888.

🔍 Most Common Scenario
You probably have something like this in config:

service:
  telemetry:
    metrics:
      address: ":8888"

exporters:
  prometheus:
    endpoint: "0.0.0.0:8888"
That creates a conflict.

✅ FIX OPTION 1 (Recommended)
Change Prometheus exporter port.

Example:

exporters:
  prometheus:
    endpoint: "0.0.0.0:8889"
Keep internal telemetry on 8888.

Then restart collector.

✅ FIX OPTION 2
Disable internal telemetry metrics completely:

service:
  telemetry:
    metrics:
      level: none
Then Prometheus can use 8888 safely.

✅ FIX OPTION 3 (If Running in Kubernetes)
If you are running via Helm (like your earlier otel release):

Check:

kubectl get pods -n observability
You might have:

One otel collector pod already running

And you're starting another manually

If so → delete old pod or stop local instance.

🔎 How to Confirm What Is Using 8888
If running locally:

sudo lsof -i :8888
or

netstat -tulnp | grep 8888
🚀 Quickest Fix For You
Since you're using Loki exporter and OTLP receiver only for logs, you probably don't even need Prometheus exporter.

Remove this completely:

exporters:
  prometheus:
and remove it from pipeline.

Restart collector.

💡 Bonus: About 0.0.0.0 Warning
This warning:

Using the 0.0.0.0 address exposes this server...
It is just security warning. Not an error.

If you want to remove warning:

Change:

endpoint: "0.0.0.0:4317"
To:

endpoint: "localhost:4317"
🎯 Final Summary
Your issue is NOT Loki
Your issue is NOT OTLP
Your issue is NOT memory limiter

👉 It is port 8888 conflict

Change one of them to different port.

If you paste your full otel-collector-config.yaml, I will tell you exactly which line to change.


