ChatGPT said:
Good 👌 now we can see the REAL problem clearly.

You have two different Prometheus metric servers running inside the same collector.

🔥 The Conflict Is Here
Inside your ConfigMap:

1️⃣ Prometheus exporter (GOOD – using 8889 ✅)
exporters:
  prometheus:
    endpoint: 0.0.0.0:8889
This is correct.

2️⃣ Service telemetry metrics (THIS is the problem ❌)
service:
  telemetry:
    metrics:
      readers:
      - pull:
          exporter:
            prometheus:
              host: ${env:MY_POD_IP}
              port: 8888
This ALSO starts a Prometheus server on 8888.

And in your logs we see:

Serving metrics {"address": "10.244.120.75:8888"}
Serving metrics {"address": ":8888"}
Then collector crashes:

listen tcp :8888: bind: address already in use
🎯 Why This Happens
In OpenTelemetry Collector:

There are TWO separate metric systems:

exporters.prometheus → your metrics pipeline

service.telemetry.metrics → internal collector metrics

You enabled BOTH.

They both try to run a Prometheus server.

That’s the port conflict.

✅ PRODUCTION CORRECT FIX
You do NOT need:

service:
  telemetry:
    metrics:
      readers:
        ...
Because you already expose metrics via:

exporters:
  prometheus:
    endpoint: 0.0.0.0:8889
🚀 Remove This Entire Block
Delete this completely:

telemetry:
  metrics:
    readers:
    - pull:
        exporter:
          prometheus:
            host: ${env:MY_POD_IP}
            port: 8888
So your service: becomes:

service:
  extensions:
  - health_check
  pipelines:
    logs:
      receivers: [otlp]
      processors: [memory_limiter, batch]
      exporters: [loki]

    metrics:
      receivers: [otlp]
      processors: [memory_limiter, batch]
      exporters: [prometheus]

    traces:
      receivers: [otlp]
      processors: [memory_limiter, batch]
      exporters: [otlp/tempo]
Nothing more.

🔁 Then Redeploy
helm upgrade otel . -n observability
or

kubectl rollout restart deployment otel-opentelemetry-collector -n observability
🎯 After Fix You Should See
No more:

listen tcp :8888: bind: address already in use
And pod will stay running.

