ChatGPT said:
Your values.yaml is correct ✅

The problem is NOT in your config section.

The problem is the Helm chart default behavior.

You are using the official Helm chart for
OpenTelemetry Collector

And starting from newer chart versions (like 0.145.0), the chart automatically enables internal telemetry unless explicitly disabled.

That is why even though you did NOT define:

service:
  telemetry:
It still appears in the rendered ConfigMap.

🎯 What Is Actually Happening
The Helm chart merges:

Your values.yaml
+
Chart default values.yaml
The chart default includes:

service:
  telemetry:
    metrics:
      readers:
        - pull:
            exporter:
              prometheus:
                host: ${env:MY_POD_IP}
                port: 8888
So Helm injects it automatically.

That’s why 8888 is still being started.

✅ Proper Fix (Production Correct Way)
You must explicitly disable the default telemetry block.

Add this to your values.yaml under config.service:

config:
  service:
    telemetry: {}
OR even better (clean disable):

config:
  service:
    telemetry:
      metrics:
        level: none
🚀 Final Correct values.yaml (Minimal Fix)
Inside your existing config.service block, change it to:

config:
  service:
    telemetry:
      metrics:
        level: none
    extensions: [health_check]
    pipelines:
      traces:
        receivers: [otlp]
        processors: [memory_limiter, batch]
        exporters: [otlp/tempo]

      logs:
        receivers: [otlp]
        processors: [memory_limiter, batch]
        exporters: [loki]

      metrics:
        receivers: [otlp]
        processors: [memory_limiter, batch]
        exporters: [prometheus]
