You said:
in my chart values.yaml and values-prod.yaml is there when we applying chart then both combine values will taken or only vales-prod.yaml is taken
note while applying chart i clealy mention values-prod.yaml

ChatGPT said:
Very important Helm concept 👌 — this confuses many DevOps engineers.

You are using Helm chart for
Helm

🎯 Short Answer
If you run:

helm upgrade otel . -n observability -f values-prod.yaml
👉 Helm will use:

Chart default values.yaml
+ values-prod.yaml
It will NOT automatically load your local values.yaml file unless you explicitly pass it.

🔍 How Helm Value Merging Works
Helm loads values in this order (lowest → highest priority):

1️⃣ Chart's internal values.yaml (inside chart package)
2️⃣ Files passed using -f (in the order provided)
3️⃣ --set flags

Later ones override earlier ones.

🚨 Important Clarification
There are TWO types of values.yaml:

1️⃣ Chart internal values.yaml
This always loads.

2️⃣ Your custom values.yaml in your folder
This loads ONLY if:

helm upgrade otel . -f values.yaml
If you only pass:

-f values-prod.yaml
Then ONLY that file overrides the chart defaults.

🧠 Example
If chart default has:

replicaCount: 1
Your values-prod.yaml has:

replicaCount: 2
Result = 2

If your local values.yaml has:

replicaCount: 3
But you run:

helm upgrade otel . -f values-prod.yaml
Then 3 is ignored.

🔥 What Probably Happened In Your Case
Your values-prod.yaml might NOT contain:

config:
  service:
    telemetry:
      metrics:
        level: none
So chart default telemetry block is still active.

✅ How To Confirm What Helm Actually Used
Run:

helm get values otel -n observability
If you want to see ALL merged values:

helm get values otel -n observability --all
This shows:

chart default
+ values-prod.yaml
= final result
🚀 Best Practice For Production
Usually we do:

values.yaml        → common config
values-prod.yaml   → production overrides
Then deploy like:

helm upgrade otel . \
  -n observability \
  -f values.yaml \
  -f values-prod.yaml
Order matters:

Later files override earlier ones.

🎯 Final Answer To Your Question
If you clearly mentioned:

-f values-prod.yaml
Then:

✔ Chart internal defaults are loaded
✔ values-prod.yaml overrides them
❌ Your other local values.yaml is ignored

If you paste your values-prod.yaml, I will verify whether telemetry block is still coming from chart defaults and fix it cleanly 🚀


