You said:

helm install otel . \\ -n observability \\ -f values.yaml

how to install using two values.yaml?

ChatGPT said:
Very simple 👍 — Helm supports multiple -f files.

✅ Install Helm Chart Using Two values Files
If you have:

values.yaml
values-prod.yaml
Run:

helm install otel . \
  -n observability \
  -f values.yaml \
  -f values-prod.yaml
🧠 How It Works (Very Important)
Helm merges in this order:

1️⃣ Chart default values.yaml (inside chart)
2️⃣ -f values.yaml
3️⃣ -f values-prod.yaml
👉 Last file wins if same key exists.

So:

values.yaml → base config

values-prod.yaml → production overrides

🔥 Example
values.yaml
replicaCount: 1
resources:
  limits:
    memory: 512Mi
values-prod.yaml
replicaCount: 3
Final result:

replicaCount = 3   ✅ (overridden)
memory = 512Mi     ✅ (kept from base)
✅ Upgrade With Two Files
For upgrade:

helm upgrade otel . \
  -n observability \
  -f values.yaml \
  -f values-prod.yaml
🔎 See Final Merged Values
After install:

helm get values otel -n observability --all
This shows final merged configuration.

🚀 Production Best Practice Pattern
Most teams structure like this:

values.yaml          → common settings
values-dev.yaml      → dev overrides
values-prod.yaml     → prod overrides
Then deploy like:

helm install otel . -f values.yaml -f values-prod.yaml
If you want, I can also show you how to structure base + prod values cleanly for your OpenTelemetry setup with Prometheus + Loki + Tempo.


