Perfect 👍 now we debug using YOUR actual Prometheus CR.

You asked about:

STEP 2 — Check Prometheus Is Watching That Namespace
What does that mean?

Now I’ll explain using your real YAML.

You are running Prometheus via:

👉 Prometheus Operator
👉 Installed through kube-prometheus-stack (Helm)

🔥 THE IMPORTANT PART IN YOUR YAML
Look carefully at this section:

serviceMonitorNamespaceSelector: {}
serviceMonitorSelector:
  matchLabels:
    release: prometheus
This is the MOST IMPORTANT part for your issue.

🧠 What This Means
1️⃣ serviceMonitorNamespaceSelector: {}
This tells Prometheus:

"Watch ServiceMonitors in ALL namespaces"

Because {} means empty selector = no restriction.

So namespace is NOT your problem ✅

Prometheus is watching:

monitoring

observability

default

everything

So STEP 2 is already correct in your setup.

2️⃣ serviceMonitorSelector:
matchLabels:
  release: prometheus
This means:

Prometheus will ONLY pick ServiceMonitors that have label:

release=prometheus
⚠️ THIS is probably your real problem.

🔥 Why Your Target Is Not Showing
If your ServiceMonitor YAML does NOT contain:

metadata:
  labels:
    release: prometheus
Then Prometheus will COMPLETELY IGNORE it.

Even if:

It exists

It is correct

Namespace is correct

Port is correct

It will NOT be picked.

🎯 Confirm Now
Run:

kubectl get servicemonitor -A --show-labels
If you do NOT see:

release=prometheus
Then that is the issue.

✅ FIX
Edit your ServiceMonitor:

apiVersion: monitoring.coreos.com/v1
kind: ServiceMonitor
metadata:
  name: otel-collector-sm
  namespace: monitoring
  labels:
    release: prometheus   # VERY IMPORTANT
spec:
  namespaceSelector:
    matchNames:
      - observability
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app.kubernetes.io/name: opentelemetry-collector
  endpoints:
    - port: metrics
Apply:

kubectl apply -f servicemonitor.yaml
Wait 30 seconds.

Then check:

Prometheus UI → Status → Targets

Now it should appear.

🧠 Why Helm Does This
Because you installed via:

kube-prometheus-stack

Helm automatically adds:

serviceMonitorSelector.matchLabels.release=prometheus
So only ServiceMonitors created by that Helm release are selected.

This prevents random ServiceMonitors from being scraped.

