Now let’s explain clearly for production DevOps.

Using:

OpenTelemetry

OpenTelemetry Collector

Loki

Grafana

🔥 1️⃣ Can OpenTelemetry Java Agent Send Logs?
YES — but only if:

You enable log instrumentation

Your logs are structured (logback/log4j2 supported)

You enable OTLP log exporter

Without that → agent only sends traces & metrics.

🔥 2️⃣ Architecture You Want
Spring Boot App
   + OTel Java Agent
        ↓ OTLP (logs, traces, metrics)
OpenTelemetry Collector
        ↓
Loki (logs)
Tempo (traces)
Prometheus (metrics)
        ↓
Grafana
This is modern approach ✅

🔥 3️⃣ What To Change In Dockerfile?
You must add OTel Java agent.

Example:

FROM eclipse-temurin:17-jdk

WORKDIR /app

# Add OpenTelemetry Java agent
ADD https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/releases/latest/download/opentelemetry-javaagent.jar /otel-agent.jar

COPY target/job-api-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar app.jar

ENTRYPOINT ["java",
 "-javaagent:/otel-agent.jar",
 "-Dotel.service.name=job-api",
 "-Dotel.exporter.otlp.endpoint=http://otel-collector.observability:4317",
 "-Dotel.logs.exporter=otlp",
 "-Dotel.metrics.exporter=otlp",
 "-Dotel.traces.exporter=otlp",
 "-jar","app.jar"]
⚠️ Use correct service DNS:

otel-collector.observability.svc.cluster.local
🔥 4️⃣ Collector Config Must Support OTLP Logs
In OTel Collector:

receivers:
  otlp:
    protocols:
      grpc:
      http:

exporters:
  loki:
    endpoint: http://loki.observability:3100/loki/api/v1/push

service:
  pipelines:
    logs:
      receivers: [otlp]
      exporters: [loki]

    traces:
      receivers: [otlp]
      exporters: [tempo]

    metrics:
      receivers: [otlp]
      exporters: [prometheus]
If logs pipeline not defined → nothing will reach Loki.

🔥 5️⃣ Is This Better Than filelog?
Let’s compare.

filelog receiver	Java Agent logs
Reads container logs	Sends structured logs directly
Simple	More modern
Works for any language	Java only
No trace correlation	TraceID auto-injected
👉 Agent approach gives automatic traceId correlation in logs.

🔥 6️⃣ VERY IMPORTANT (Common Mistake)
Java agent does NOT automatically send logs unless:

You enable:

-Dotel.logs.exporter=otlp
AND

Your logging framework supports OpenTelemetry log appender.

For Spring Boot (logback), you may need logback config.

🔥 7️⃣ How To Verify It Works
In Prometheus:

otelcol_receiver_accepted_log_records
In Grafana (Loki datasource):

{service_name="job-api"}
If logs appear → success.

🚨 Production Reality
Most companies use:

Java Agent → traces & metrics

Fluentbit / Promtail → logs

Because logs via agent still evolving.

But full OTLP pipeline is modern cloud-native approach.

🎯 Final Answer
YES ✅ you can do:

App + OTel Java Agent → OTel Collector → Loki → Grafana
But:

Collector must have logs pipeline

Agent must enable logs exporter

Logging framework must be compatible

