ChatGPT said:
Perfect 👍 this error is very clear.

❌ Root Cause
ClassNotFoundException: net.logstash.logback.encoder.LogstashEncoder
Means:

👉 Your logback-spring.xml is using:

<encoder class="net.logstash.logback.encoder.LogstashEncoder"/>
BUT

🚨 The dependency logstash-logback-encoder is NOT in your classpath.

I checked your classpath in the log — and I do NOT see:

net/logstash/logback/logstash-logback-encoder
So Maven dependency is missing.

✅ Correct Fix (100% Working)
Step 1 — Add Dependency in pom.xml
Add this EXACT block:

<dependency>
    <groupId>net.logstash.logback</groupId>
    <artifactId>logstash-logback-encoder</artifactId>
    <version>7.4</version>
</dependency>
Put it inside <dependencies>.

Step 2 — Clean & Rebuild
Very important ⚠️

Run:

mvn clean install
OR in IntelliJ:

Maven → Reload Project
Then run again.

🔎 Why It Happened
You are using:

Spring Boot 4.0.3

Java 22

Spring Boot 4 is VERY NEW.

It does NOT auto-manage logstash-logback-encoder.

So if dependency not present → ClassNotFoundException.

🧠 How To Verify It Is Fixed
After adding dependency:

Run:

mvn dependency:tree | grep logstash
You should see:

net.logstash.logback:logstash-logback-encoder:7.4
If not → dependency not loaded.

⚠️ One More Important Thing
Your log shows:

spring-boot-starter 4.0.3
Spring Boot 4 is still very new.

For production company setup I strongly recommend:

👉 Use Spring Boot 3.2.x (stable LTS style usage)

Unless you intentionally want Boot 4.

🚀 After Fix
When it works you will see logs like:

{
  "@timestamp": "2026-02-16T08:30:00.123Z",
