ChatGPT said:
Perfect 👍 this is simple Dockerfile syntax mistake.

❌ Why This Error Happened
Error:

dockerfile parse error: unknown instruction: "-javaagent:otel-agent.jar"
Docker thinks:

"-javaagent:otel-agent.jar"
is a NEW Docker instruction.

Why?
Because your ENTRYPOINT JSON array is broken across lines incorrectly.

Dockerfile JSON array must be valid JSON.

❌ Your Wrong Format (Probably Like This)
ENTRYPOINT ["java",
 "-javaagent:otel-agent.jar",
 "-Dotel.service.name=job-api",
 "-Dotel.exporter.otlp.endpoint=http://otel-collector.observability:4317",
 "-jar","app.jar"]
If comma or quote missing → Docker parse error.

✅ Correct Working Dockerfile (With OTel Agent)
Here is 100% working production-safe version:

FROM eclipse-temurin:17-jdk

WORKDIR /app

COPY target/job-api-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar app.jar
COPY opentelemetry-javaagent.jar otel-agent.jar

ENTRYPOINT ["java",
"-javaagent:/app/otel-agent.jar",
"-Dotel.service.name=job-api",
"-Dotel.exporter.otlp.endpoint=http://otel-collector.observability:4317",
"-Dotel.exporter.otlp.protocol=grpc",
"-jar","/app/app.jar"]
🔥 Important Fixes
1️⃣ Always use FULL PATH for javaagent
-javaagent:/app/otel-agent.jar
Not relative.

2️⃣ Make Sure Agent File Exists
Your project folder must contain:

opentelemetry-javaagent.jar
If not → download from:

