--------------------
ERROR: failed to solve: dockerfile parse error on line 11: unknown instruction: "-javaagent:/app/otel-agent.jar",

ChatGPT said:
Good 👍 this error now clearly tells one thing:

👉 Your ENTRYPOINT JSON array is NOT properly closed on previous line.

Docker is treating:

"-javaagent:/app/otel-agent.jar",
as a new Docker instruction.

That only happens when:

Previous line missing ]

OR previous line missing \

OR using wrong quotes

OR there is a hidden character

🔥 100% Safe Solution (Use Shell Form Instead)
Instead of JSON array (exec form), use shell form.

This avoids JSON parsing issues.

✅ Use This Dockerfile (Guaranteed Working)
FROM eclipse-temurin:17-jdk

WORKDIR /app

COPY target/job-api-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar app.jar
COPY opentelemetry-javaagent.jar otel-agent.jar

ENTRYPOINT java \
 -javaagent:/app/otel-agent.jar \
 -Dotel.service.name=job-api \
 -Dotel.exporter.otlp.endpoint=http://otel-opentelemetry-collector:4317 \
 -Dotel.exporter.otlp.protocol=grpc \
 -jar /app/app.jar
⚠️ Notice:

No quotes

No JSON array

Using \ line continuation

Clean shell format

🧠 Why This Works
Docker supports 2 ENTRYPOINT formats:

1️⃣ Exec form (JSON array)
ENTRYPOINT ["java", "-jar", "app.jar"]
2️⃣ Shell form
ENTRYPOINT java -jar app.jar
Your JSON form keeps breaking.

Shell form = safer for long Java args.

🚀 After Fix
Run:

docker build -t job-api .
It WILL build.

⚠️ If Still Fails
Then problem is:

Windows CRLF line endings

Hidden characters

Wrong indentation before ENTRYPOINT

Run this to fix line endings:

dos2unix Dockerfile
Then build again.

